=== P2 Widget primitive 0009 WidgetRankedList (Windows) ===

Capability: WinUI 3 (Windows App SDK) + .NET 10 present on this runner (dotnet 10.0.300;
net10.0-windows10.0.19041.0 app TFM). Build + headless logic tests run here. The E2E UI-automation
runner (WinAppDriver/Appium) is ABSENT on this non-interactive host — see the TEST step.

Web source (THE spec): web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/shared/WidgetRankedList.tsx — a pure
presentational widget primitive (no hooks / no data sources). Props: items, maxItems, compact(false),
showBars(true), emptyMessage('No data available'), emptyIcon. RankedItem: id, label, value,
formattedValue, badge?{text, variant: success|warning|error|neutral}, barColor?(Tailwind class).
Derivations: limit = maxItems ?? (compact ? 3 : 5); hideBars = compact || !showBars;
visible = [...items].sort((a,b)=>b.value-a.value).slice(0,limit); maxValue = reduce(Math.max, seed 0);
empty branch (visible.length===0) → <EmptyState icon message py-8>; row branch → rank(i+1), background
bar (barPct = maxValue>0 ? value/maxValue*100 : 0, opacity-15, color barColor ?? bg-blue-400),
truncating label, optional <Badge variant={badgeVariantMap[variant]} size="sm">, semibold value.
Shared components used (mapped to native): @/components/ui Badge → TsBadge; @/components/feedback
EmptyState → TsEmptyState.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE IMPLEMENTATION (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/widget-primitives/WidgetRankedList.*)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two-file split mirroring the shipped pure-presentational ScoreBadge surface (Model + view; no
Source/ViewModel because the web component is synchronous and prop-driven — its parent widget owns any
fetching):
  .Model.cs  - Microsoft.UI-free. WidgetRankedListRegistration (slug "WidgetRankedList");
               RankedBadgeVariant enum (success/warning/error/neutral — the web RankedItem.badge.variant
               union); RankedBadge + RankedItem (id/label/value/formattedValue/badge/barColorHex) input
               records; WidgetRankedListModel (items/maxItems/compact/showBars/emptyMessage/
               emptyIconGlyph, null-safe Items default + Empty); WidgetRankedListProjection — the native
               port of the web body: LimitFor (maxItems ?? compact?3:5), StatusFor (badgeVariantMap,
               error→Danger), descending STABLE sort + Take(max(0,limit)), zero-seeded maxValue
               (reduce(Math.max,0)), barPercent = value/maxValue*100 clamped to the 0..100 a browser
               actually paints, default bar tint #60a5fa (Tailwind blue-400 = web bg-blue-400), localized
               empty message + composed per-row accessible name; WidgetRankedListDisplay / RankedRow /
               RankedBadgeDisplay projections; PII-safe WidgetRankedListDiagnostics (view.opened only).
  .cs        - WinUI 3 ContentControl view. Empty branch → TsEmptyState (message + optional glyph; never
               a blank box). List branch → ScrollViewer(overflow-y-auto) over a StackPanel(gap-1) of row
               Grids: each row is min-h 44, rounded(TsRadiusSm), tokenized hover surface
               (TsColorSurfaceGlassBrush = web hover:bg-[var(--surface-2)]); a declarative two
               star-column bar track (barPercent : 100-barPercent) hosts the opacity-15 tinted Border
               (DisplayPrimitives.HexBrush — semantic data-attribute colour); the content grid carries
               the right-aligned rank (muted), truncating label (CharacterEllipsis), optional sm TsBadge
               (status-mapped) and semibold value. Tokens via DisplayTokens (TextMuted/TextPrimary).
               Emits view.opened on Loaded.

States reproduced from the web source (every state the source has renders; none hidden):
  populated list | empty (always-rendered EmptyState with the localized default, a caller override, or
  the supplied glyph). NOTE: the web source is a PURE PRESENTATIONAL primitive with no hooks — it has
  exactly two render branches and NO fetch-driven loading / error / stale / offline branch. Per the
  shipped sibling ScoreBadge precedent (same template, same "no fetch states" finding), those generic
  states are NOT fabricated — faithful parity reproduces the two real branches. Honesty covenant rule 2
  (no scope narrowing) / rule 5 (no parity shortcuts): the spec's states checklist is satisfied by the
  branches that exist in THE spec; inventing absent chrome would be silent drift.

i18n (P1/S10): every string flows through ILocalizer.GetString(key, fallback). Keys (+ English
  fallbacks verbatim from the web): widgets.rankedList.emptyDefault ("No data available", the web
  default prop), widgets.rankedList.rowAccessibleName ("{{rank}}. {{label}}, {{value}}"),
  widgets.rankedList.rowAccessibleNameWithBadge ("{{rank}}. {{label}}, {{value}} ({{badge}})"). No
  English literals in native code.
A11y: each row carries a composed Narrator name (rank + label + value + badge); the bar, rank, label,
  badge and value sub-elements are marked AccessibilityView.Raw so the row announces once; the list is
  exposed as Content. TsEmptyState announces its message via its live region. System font scale +
  reduced-motion inherit from the shared primitives.
Telemetry: view.opened slug=WidgetRankedList on Loaded (P1/S11), PII-safe (never row labels or values).
Tests (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/WidgetPrimitives/WidgetRankedListTests.cs — 40 methods / 43
  cases): adapter unit tests (limit matrix; descending + STABLE-sort ordering; bar percent proportional
  / zero-seeded all-negative / clamped; show-hide-bars matrix; default vs custom vs blank bar colour;
  badge variant→status mapping incl. error→danger), per-state tests (populated rows; empty default /
  override / icon passthrough / zero & negative maxItems → empty), a11y-label tests (composed row name
  with + without badge, token-leak guard, rank reflects sorted position), registration, PII-safe
  diagnostics, and null-safety / argument guards. All via PassthroughLocalizer, headless (no UI host).

